plan.text:
{"t":"scope","verdict":"in","reason":"Quadratic vertices are core algebra."}
{"t":"objective","text":"Find the vertex of a parabola from its roots using symmetry."}
{"t":"warmup","id":"w1","prompt":"What is the midpoint of 1 and 3?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"2","correct":true},{"id":"b","text":"4","correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"1.5","correct":false}]}
{"t":"segment","n":1,"title":"Roots and symmetry","goal":"Use the roots to find the axis of symmetry and the vertex.","representation":"graph","misconception":"Vertex x-value comes from the constant term.","check":"choice"}
{"t":"segment","n":2,"title":"Completing the picture","goal":"Connect the vertex to the minimum value.","representation":"worked","misconception":"The vertex is always on the y-axis.","check":"number"}

segment:1.text:
{"t":"say","text":"Let's find where the curve y = x² − 4x + 3 crosses the x-axis, since that reveals the vertex."}
{"t":"math","id":"eq1","latex":"y = x^2 - 4x + 3","expr":"y=x^2-4*x+3"}
{"t":"say","text":"Set y to zero and factor: we need two numbers multiplying to 3 and adding to −4."}
{"t":"math","id":"fac","latex":"x^2 - 4x + 3 = (x-1)(x-3) = 0","expr":"(x-1)*(x-3)=0"}
{"t":"say","text":"Each bracket can be zero, so the roots are x = 1 and x = 3."}
{"t":"solutions","id":"roots","of":"fac","var":"x","values":[1,3],"latex":"x = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = 3"}
{"t":"mark","kind":"underline","target":"roots","note":"where the curve meets the x-axis"}
{"t":"say","text":"Here is the graph, with both roots marked on the x-axis."}
{"t":"plot","id":"p1","x":[-1,5],"y":[-2,6],"fns":[{"id":"f1","expr":"x^2-4*x+3","label":"y = x² − 4x + 3"}]}
{"t":"point","plot":"p1","id":"r1","at":[1,0],"label":"(1, 0)"}
{"t":"point","plot":"p1","id":"r2","at":[3,0],"label":"(3, 0)"}
{"t":"say","text":"A parabola is symmetric, so its axis of symmetry sits exactly halfway between the two roots."}
{"t":"math","id":"axis","latex":"x = \\frac{1+3}{2} = 2","expr":"x=(1+3)/2"}
{"t":"say","text":"The vertex lies on that axis, so its x-coordinate is 2. Substitute to find y."}
{"t":"math","id":"sub","latex":"y = 2^2 - 4(2) + 3 = 4 - 8 + 3 = -1","expr":"2^2-4*2+3"}
{"t":"point","plot":"p1","id":"v","at":[2,-1],"label":"Vertex (2, −1)"}
{"t":"mark","kind":"circle","target":"v","note":"lowest point, on the axis x = 2"}
{"t":"say","text":"So the vertex is (2, −1). Quick check: which statement explains why the vertex has x = 2?"}
{"t":"check","id":"c1","kind":"choice","prompt":"Why is the x-coordinate of the vertex equal to 2?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It is halfway between the roots 1 and 3, because the parabola is symmetric.","correct":true,"misconception":""},{"id":"b","text":"It is the constant term 3 minus 1.","correct":false,"misconception":"Believes the vertex x-value comes from combining the constant term with a root, rather than from symmetry."},{"id":"c","text":"It is the x-value where the curve crosses the y-axis.","correct":false,"misconception":"Confuses the y-intercept (x = 0, y = 3) with the vertex."},{"id":"d","text":"It is half of the coefficient −4, so x = −2.","correct":false,"misconception":"Halves the coefficient of x but forgets the sign change, so uses −b/2 incorrectly as b/2."}],"explain":"Right: a parabola is symmetric, so its vertex sits halfway between the two roots.","hint":"Think about the symmetry of the curve and where the two roots sit."}

segment:2.text:
{"t":"say","text":"The vertex is the lowest point, so its y-value is the smallest value the curve reaches."}
{"t":"math","id":"minv","latex":"y_{\\min} = -1"}
{"t":"say","text":"Check another point: at x = 0 the height is 3, which is higher."}
{"t":"math","id":"at0","latex":"y = 0^2 - 4(0) + 3 = 3","expr":"0^2-4*0+3"}
{"t":"ask","id":"q2","text":"Why is the vertex the lowest point?"}
{"t":"say","text":"Quick check: what is the minimum value of y?"}
{"t":"check","id":"c2","kind":"number","prompt":"What is the minimum value of y on this parabola?","answer":"-1","tolerance":0,"anticipated":[{"value":"2","misconception":"Gives the x-coordinate of the vertex instead of its y-value."}],"explain":"Right: the vertex height is the minimum, so y = -1.","hint":"Look at the height of the vertex, not its position along the x-axis."}

reteach:c1:b.text:
{"t":"say","text":"Close, but 3 is where the curve crosses the y-axis, not where it is symmetric."}
{"t":"math","id":"rb1","latex":"x = \\frac{1+3}{2} = 2","expr":"x=(1+3)/2"}
{"t":"say","text":"Halfway between the roots is 2, and symmetry puts the vertex on that line."}

reteach:c1:c.text:
{"t":"say","text":"The y-axis crossing happens where x is 0, which gives a height of 3."}
{"t":"math","id":"rc1","latex":"y = 0^2 - 4(0) + 3 = 3","expr":"0^2-4*0+3"}
{"t":"say","text":"That point is not the lowest one, so it cannot be the vertex."}
{"t":"say","text":"The vertex sits halfway between the roots 1 and 3, so x = 2."}

reteach:c1:d.text:
{"t":"say","text":"Halving the coefficient is close, but the sign flips: the axis is at negative b over two a."}
{"t":"math","id":"rd1","latex":"x = -\\frac{-4}{2(1)} = 2","expr":"x=-(-4)/(2*1)"}
{"t":"say","text":"That agrees with the midpoint of the roots, so the vertex has x = 2."}

solution:c1.text:
{"t":"say","text":"Here is the answer: the roots are 1 and 3, so the axis sits halfway between them."}
{"t":"math","id":"sc1","latex":"x = \\frac{1+3}{2} = 2","expr":"x=(1+3)/2"}
{"t":"say","text":"The vertex lies on that axis, so its x-coordinate is 2."}

reteach:c2:a0.text:
{"t":"say","text":"You found the x-coordinate 2. The question asks for the height at that point."}
{"t":"math","id":"ra1","latex":"y = 2^2 - 4(2) + 3 = -1","expr":"2^2-4*2+3"}
{"t":"say","text":"Height means y, so the minimum value is negative one."}

reteach:c2:other.text:
{"t":"say","text":"Try again: put x = 2 into the equation and read off the height."}
{"t":"math","id":"ro1","latex":"y = 4 - 8 + 3 = -1","expr":"4-8+3"}
{"t":"say","text":"Every other point on the curve is higher than that."}

solution:c2.text:
{"t":"say","text":"The lowest point is the vertex, and its height is the minimum value."}
{"t":"math","id":"sc2","latex":"y_{\\min} = 2^2 - 4(2) + 3 = -1","expr":"2^2-4*2+3"}
{"t":"say","text":"So the minimum value of y is negative one."}

lost:1:1.text:
{"t":"say","text":"Let me say it more simply: the curve is a mirror image on both sides of a line."}
{"t":"math","id":"l11","latex":"x = \\frac{1+3}{2} = 2","expr":"x=(1+3)/2"}
{"t":"say","text":"That mirror line passes through the vertex, halfway between the roots."}

lost:2:1.text:
{"t":"say","text":"Think of the vertex as the bottom of a bowl: nothing on the curve goes lower."}
{"t":"math","id":"l21","latex":"y = 2^2 - 4(2) + 3 = -1","expr":"2^2-4*2+3"}
{"t":"say","text":"That height, negative one, is the smallest value of y."}

answer:q2.text:
{"t":"say","text":"The curve opens upward, so it falls to the vertex and then rises again."}
{"t":"math","id":"aq1","latex":"y = (x-2)^2 - 1","expr":"y=(x-2)^2-1"}
{"t":"say","text":"A square is never negative, so y is smallest when the bracket is zero."}

recap.text:
{"t":"idea","id":"i1","text":"The vertex sits halfway between the roots, on the axis of symmetry.","seg":1}
{"t":"idea","id":"i2","text":"The height of the vertex is the minimum value of the parabola.","seg":2}
{"t":"say","text":"Let us try a few on your own."}
{"t":"check","id":"rp1","kind":"choice","prompt":"A parabola has roots at 2 and 6. What is the x-coordinate of its vertex?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"4","correct":true},{"id":"b","text":"8","correct":false,"misconception":"Adds the roots instead of halving the sum."},{"id":"c","text":"2","correct":false,"misconception":"Uses a root instead of the midpoint."}],"explain":"Halfway between 2 and 6 is 4.","hint":"The axis is midway between the roots.","idea":"i1"}
{"t":"check","id":"rp2","kind":"number","prompt":"A parabola has roots at 0 and 8. What is the x-coordinate of its vertex?","answer":"4","tolerance":0,"explain":"Halfway between 0 and 8 is 4.","hint":"Add the roots and halve.","idea":"i1"}
{"t":"check","id":"rp3","kind":"number","prompt":"y = x^2 - 4x + 3 has its vertex at (2, -1). What is its minimum value?","answer":"-1","tolerance":0,"anticipated":[{"value":"2","misconception":"Gives the x-coordinate of the vertex instead of its y-value."}],"explain":"The vertex height is the minimum, so -1.","hint":"Which coordinate is the height?","idea":"i2"}
